---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Zero Bite Support" description="Help with Zero Bite: scanning, reminders, recipes, food recall alerts and your data." section="zerobite">
  <p class="overline">Support</p>
  <h1>How can we help?</h1>
  <p class="lead">Email <a href="mailto:support@mazesys.com?subject=Zero%20Bite%20support">support@mazesys.com</a> and we'll get back to you, usually within two working days. It helps to include your iPhone model and iOS version.</p>

  <h2>Scanning labels</h2>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>The date wasn't read correctly</strong>
  <p>Hold the phone steady with the date filling the frame, in good light, and avoid glare on shiny packaging. On the review screen you can pick a different date it found, or choose “None of these” and set the date yourself.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>The product name didn't fill in</strong>
  <p>Names come from Open Food Facts, a free community database. Supermarket own-brand products are sometimes missing; type the name in and it'll be saved with your item.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>I don't see “Scan with the camera”</strong>
  <p>Live scanning needs an iPhone with the A12 chip or newer and camera access. You can turn camera access on in the Settings app → Zero Bite. You can always choose a photo of the label instead.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reminders</h2>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>I'm not getting reminders</strong>
  <p>Check Zero Bite → Settings → Expiry reminders is on, and that notifications are allowed in the Settings app → Notifications → Zero Bite. Use “Send a test notification” to check. Reminders arrive at the time you choose, a set number of days before the date.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Food recall alerts</h2>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>How does Zero Bite know about recalls?</strong>
  <p>It downloads the Food Standards Agency's public recall and allergy alerts for the UK and compares them with what's in your fridge, using the product name, brand, barcode and batch dates.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>Why does it say “possible recall”?</strong>
  <p>Recall notices rarely include barcodes, so matches are a warning to check, not a certainty. Compare the batch code and date on your pack with the notice. If it isn't affected, tap “Not my batch” and we won't flag it again.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>Allergy alerts</strong>
  <p>Choose your allergies in Settings → Your allergies. Allergy alerts for those allergens appear under Food alerts → For you. Zero Bite is not a substitute for reading labels or medical advice.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>Is my food list backed up?</strong>
  <p>Your list is stored on your iPhone and included in your normal iPhone backups. There's no Zero Bite account, so it isn't stored anywhere else.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
  <strong>How do I delete everything?</strong>
  <p>Go to Settings → Data → Delete everything, or delete the app. See the <a href="/zerobite/privacy-policy.html">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
